     "text": "Certainly! Based on the latest coding guidelines provided by your mentor, here is a `NearestNeighbors` model class that includes `train` and `predict` methods. The implementation follows best practices for Python code structure, readability, and maintainability, including proper use of type hints, docstrings, and encapsulation.\n\n```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Any, Optional\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors as SklearnNearestNeighbors\n\nclass NearestNeighbors:\n    \"\"\"\n    A Nearest Neighbors model for classification and regression tasks.\n    \n    This class provides a simple interface to the scikit-learn Nearest Neighbors algorithm.\n    It includes methods for training the model and making predictions.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, n_neighbors: int = 5, metric: str = 'euclidean'):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the Nearest Neighbors model.\n\n        Parameters:\n        n_neighbors (int): Number of neighbors to consider.\n        metric (str): Metric to use for distance calculation.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.n_neighbors = n_neighbors\n        self.metric = metric\n        self._model: Optional[SklearnNearestNeighbors] = None\n\n    def train(self, X: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Train the Nearest Neighbors model.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X (np.ndarray): Training data, shape (n_samples, n_features).\n        y (np.ndarray): Target labels, shape (n_samples,).\n        \"\"\"\n        if X.shape[0] == 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Training data must not be empty.\")\n        if y.shape[0] != X.shape[0]:\n            raise ValueError(\"Training data and target labels must have the same number of samples.\")\n\n        self._model = SklearnNearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=self.n_neighbors, metric=self.metric)\n        self._model.fit(X, y)\n\n    def predict(self, X: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        \"\"\"\n        Predict the target labels for the given input data.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X (np.ndarray): Input data, shape (n_samples, n_features).\n\n        Returns:\n        np.ndarray: Predicted target labels, shape (n_samples,).\n        \"\"\"\n        if X.shape[0] == 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input data must not be empty.\")\n        if self._model is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"Model has not been trained yet.\")\n\n        return self._model.predict(X)\n```\n\n### Key Features",
